<p>Hazel Green has history that affects its homes. Longtime residents remember the 1974 tornado outbreak that cut through this area — an F5 that devastated parts of the community. That history shows in the housing stock: pre-1974 homes that survived, post-1974 rebuilds, and newer construction that's arrived with the growth spreading north from Huntsville.</p>

<p>Each generation of housing has its own gutter challenges. The older homes often have undersized systems from an era before modern drainage standards. The 1970s-80s rebuilds typically have sectional aluminum gutters that are now 40+ years old and past their prime. And the newer construction — especially in the subdivisions along Highway 231 — usually has builder-grade gutters that look fine but perform poorly.</p>

<p>The soil in Hazel Green is typical Madison County clay, but some areas near the Flint River corridor have slightly different drainage characteristics. Knowing which is which helps us design systems that actually work for your specific property.</p>
