<p>Practical advice for Hazel Green homeowners:</p>

<p><strong>Your home's era matters.</strong> Pre-1974 homes often have undersized gutters. 1970s-80s homes usually have aging sectional gutters with failing seams. Post-2000 homes typically have builder-grade systems that need upgrading within 10 years. Knowing your home's generation helps you anticipate problems.</p>

<p><strong>Tree debris is constant.</strong> Hazel Green's wooded lots mean gutters fill up fast. If you're surrounded by mature trees, twice-yearly cleaning is the minimum — and gutter guards are worth serious consideration.</p>

<p><strong>Watch the state line weather.</strong> The Tennessee Valley funnels storms through this area. When weather moves northeast along the valley, Hazel Green often catches more than Huntsville proper. Make sure your gutters can handle intense rainfall, not just moderate rain.</p>

